From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:41:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] smarc-rzv2l: drop legacy CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND define

The board header re-defines the CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND macro after the
Kconfig-generated value, so the vendor "env default -a;run
bootcmd_check;run bootimage" flow silently wins over any
CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND set in a defconfig or config fragment. Fresh media
with an erased environment then boots the legacy raw Image path
instead of the distro's signed-FIT boot command. Drop the define; the
Kconfig value now reaches the built-in default environment. The
vendor env scripts (bootcmd_check, emmcload, sd1load, bootimage) stay
available for manual use.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific configuration]
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-fable-5
---
 include/configs/smarc-rzv2l.h | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

--- a/include/configs/smarc-rzv2l.h
+++ b/include/configs/smarc-rzv2l.h
@@ -55,8 +55,6 @@
 	"sd1load=ext4load mmc 1:2 0x48080000 boot/Image;ext4load mmc 1:2 0x48000000 boot/r9a07g054l2-smarc.dtb;run prodsdbootargs \0" \
 	"bootcmd_check=if mmc dev 1; then run sd1load; else run emmcload; fi \0"
 
-#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND	"env default -a;run bootcmd_check;run bootimage"
-
 /* For board */
 /* Ethernet RAVB */
 #define CONFIG_BITBANGMII_MULTI
